  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe link accepts one client at a time. During a slow `camcraft-cli --ui call`, a second CLI's hello times out after 5 s.\n\nThe second CLI then reports \"the link files ... are stale\" with exit 3. A window is running.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe message names the wrong cause. The user may delete a live link or restart the window.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen a hello times out and the discovery file is fresh, print a distinct message and exit code: \"the window is busy with another call\".\n\n## Scope\n\nFound in the review of #3861 (`crates/app/src/mcp/listen.rs:233-254`, `crates/app/src/mcp/link_client.rs:181-184`). The one-client-at-a-time rule itself is accepted in `docs/decisions/3751-cli-ui-link.md`.\n",
